// Process control (M6 Task 10).
//
// `exit(code)` is a builtin, not a function in this module: the name lives in
// the one shared scope, so a wrapper would be a duplicate definition. It ends
// the process with `code` and has type `!`, so it can stand where a value is
// expected and the code after it is unreachable.
//
// `os.exit_with(code)` is the statement-shaped wrapper for a program that does
// not want to think about `!`.
//
// Ownership: `exit` never returns and owns nothing.
